WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.212
About ten kilometres above your head,

2
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:03.280
there are rivers of wind,

3
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.952
moving faster than a train.

4
00:00:04.952 --> 00:00:06.819
They're called jet streams.

5
00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:09.135
A jet stream is a narrow band

6
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:11.317
of very fast wind near the top

7
00:00:11.317 --> 00:00:12.873
of the lower atmosphere.

8
00:00:12.873 --> 00:00:14.638
It forms where warm and cold air

9
00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:17.238
meet, and the bigger the difference,

10
00:00:17.238 --> 00:00:18.897
the faster it blows.

11
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:21.816
Over India, the westerly jet blows faster

12
00:00:21.816 --> 00:00:23.569
in winter than in summer,

13
00:00:23.569 --> 00:00:25.357
at well over a hundred and fifty

14
00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:26.795
kilometres an hour.

15
00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:29.738
In winter, the subtropical westerly jet runs

16
00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:32.013
just south of the Himalayas.

17
00:00:32.013 --> 00:00:34.033
It brings in the western disturbances that

18
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.040
give the north its winter rain.

19
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.380
By early June,

20
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.215
the westerly jet shifts north of the

21
00:00:39.215 --> 00:00:42.651
Himalayas, and an easterly jet appears over

22
00:00:42.651 --> 00:00:44.404
the peninsula.

23
00:00:44.404 --> 00:00:46.924
Many scientists link this switch to the

24
00:00:46.924 --> 00:00:48.814
sudden burst of the monsoon.

25
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.049
Pilots use jet streams too.

26
00:00:51.049 --> 00:00:52.350
Flying with one saves fuel;

27
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.159
flying against it takes longer.

28
00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:56.184
For GS One:

29
00:00:56.184 --> 00:00:59.006
the westerly jet brings winter rain;

30
00:00:59.006 --> 00:00:59.958
its move north,

31
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:01.072
and the easterly jet,

32
00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:02.661
are tied to the monsoon.

